# Auth and invitations

## Identities

- **Verified**: Auth.js magic-link / email path; may have personal Game Ledger
- **Guest**: table-scoped play name + `jetonbro.guest` cookie; no email; no cross-table ledger; cannot create tables
- Roles come from snapshot flags (`isOwner`, `isDealer`, `isSeatedPlayer`) — never from name or email

## Cookies and requests

- On a table-scoped request, a **matching guest cookie wins** over Auth.js (`resolveActorFromIdentities`)
- Table page, snapshot, stream, and command routes must forward the request `Cookie` header into `getActor`
- Guest join sets the cookie and navigates with a full document load so the cookie is sent
- `GET /api/tables/{id}/snapshot` is `Cache-Control: no-store`

## Join intents

Two reusable QR join URLs with different intents:

- Guest: `/join/guest/{token}` — play name, table-scoped cookie, starting jetons once
- Verified: `/join/verified/{token}` — Auth.js magic link; multiple verified users may redeem; one membership each
- Email invitations use the verified path
- Guest QR and Verified QR are never shown as the same simultaneous primary method without exclusivity
- Join/membership changes bump `Table.updatedAt` so Owner/Dealer snapshots refresh

## Credits and idempotency

- Starting jetons credit once per membership (`starting-jetons:{tableId}:{userId}` + `startingJetonsCredited`)
- Redeem/join retries must not create a second membership or double-credit
- First-table join uses `INITIAL_ALLOCATION`

## Production constraints

- `ALLOW_DEV_MAILBOX` is local/CI only and ignored when `NODE_ENV=production`
- `/api/dev/*` always 404s in production
- Real email uses Resend HTTP API (`RESEND_API_KEY` + `EMAIL_FROM`); API key never in a URL
- Development mailbox only when `NODE_ENV !== "production"` and `ALLOW_DEV_MAILBOX=true`
- `AUTH_URL` is the public origin for magic links and invites — never `localhost` or `*.railway.internal` in production redirects
- Admin Home `WIPE ALL TABLES` is gated by exact match of verified email to server-side `JETONBRO_ADMIN_EMAIL` (never expose that email to the client)
